course: dictionary
lesson: 2402
title: A word with two jobs
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words can name a thing in one sentence and show an action in another. Cushion is one of these words. Look at the words around it to find its job. In «Rat and Mole were repairing cushions», cushions names soft things, so it is a noun.
explain: Cushion can also be a doing word. In «Grass can cushion a fall», cushion means to make a fall softer. Check it by swapping in soften: «Grass can soften a fall» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Clues in the sentence tell you which meaning to use. «He shoved the tablet under a cushion» shows a cushion is soft and can hide things. Words like sofa, fall and bump point you towards the right meaning every time.
fact: A cushion is a soft bag filled with stuffing, used to make a seat more comfortable or to lean on.
fact: «Cushion» can also mean something that makes a hit or fall softer, as in «a cushion of air».
fact: As a verb, to cushion means to make a blow or fall softer. Its forms are cushions, cushioned and cushioning.
fact: Sofa cushions and chairs are everyday examples, and foam or landing mats in gym work the same way: they cushion falls.
exercise: «So they piled cushions on the floor and called it the VIP section.» What are the cushions? | Small boxes with lids | *Soft bags filled with stuffing, for sitting or leaning on | Tall poles | Hard metal plates for the floor
exercise: In «Grass can cushion a fall», what does cushion mean? | To paint a fall | To count the falls | *To make a fall softer | To make a fall faster
exercise: Find and copy one word from this sentence that names something soft to sit or lean on: «Rat and Mole were repairing cushions.» | boat-hooks | repairing | Mole | *cushions
test: «The Knave of Hearts carried the King's crown on a crimson velvet cushion.» What is the cushion here? | A kind of cake | A hard metal tray | A loud whistle | *A soft bag filled with stuffing, used to rest the crown on
test: In «a cushion of air», what does cushion mean? | A heavy box | *Something that makes a hit or fall softer | A sharp point | A hard, flat floor
exam: Which sentence uses cushion as a verb? | «Rat and Mole were repairing cushions.» | *«Grass can cushion a fall.» | «He shoved the tablet under a cushion.»
